{"step_index":18,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T21:50:48Z","input_tokens":7006,"cache_read_tokens":42113,"output_tokens":1105,"thinking":"The PowerShell `foreach` loop syntax was reviewed for errors. Then, a detailed examination of registry properties for several `VID` and `PID` combinations was initiated to understand their characteristics.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$targets = @('VID_18D1&PID_0D02','VID_18D1&PID_4E41','VID_18D1&PID_4EE1','VID_18D1&PID_4EE7','VID_1B8E&PID_C003','VID_1B8E&PID_C004','ROOT_HUB30','VID_0000&PID_0002','VID_0000&PID_0004')\n$out = foreach ($t in $targets) {\n  $path = \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Enum\\USB\\$t\"\n  if (Test-Path $path) {\n    $sub = Get-ChildItem $path | Select-Object -First 2\n    foreach ($s in $sub) {\n      $p = Get-ItemProperty $s.PSPath\n      [PSCustomObject]@{\n        Key = \"$t\\$($s.PSChildName)\"\n        DeviceDesc = $p.DeviceDesc\n        FriendlyName = $p.FriendlyName\n        HardwareID = ($p.HardwareID -join '; ')\n        CompatibleIDs = ($p.CompatibleIDs -join '; ')\n        Service = $p.Service\n        Class = $p.Class\n        ClassGUID = $p.ClassGUID\n        Driver = $p.Driver\n        Mfg = $p.Mfg\n        LocationInformation = $p.LocationInformation\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n$out | Format-List","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Get registry details of USB devices and hubs"}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"bcdedit; Get-ItemProperty 'HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\usbflags\\*' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object PSChildName, osvc, SkipContainerIdQuery, IgnoreHWSerNum*; Get-ChildItem 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\DriverStore\\FileRepository' | Where-Object { $_.Name -match 'android|winusb|worldcup|libusb|usb|wpd|mtp|sunrise|thunderbolt|tbt' } | Select-Object Name, LastWriteTime","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Check bcdedit, usbflags, and DriverStore packag